# Content and UI kit

Copy, URLs, entity details, nav, FAQs, and form options live in `src/content/`. Components render that data. Do not hardcode ACN, support email, login URL, or legal body copy in JSX.

Legal documents are data (`src/content/legal/`) rendered by `LegalPage`. Do not add `LegalH2` / `LegalP` public helpers. Change title size, grid, or meta rail in `LegalPage` only.

## UI kit (use these — do not invent section-specific names)

**Layout** (`Container`, `.container`, `.section`, `.stack`, `.inset`)
- `Container` — centered measure + horizontal padding
- `.section` — vertical section padding
- `.stack` — vertical gap between blocks
- `.inset` — horizontal padding only (nav)
- Full-bleed blocks (Hero, film stills, testimonials) stay unpadded

**Type roles** (CSS classes — not per-section names)
- `.eyebrow` · `.heading` · `.heading-sm` · `.lead` · `.body` · `.caption`
- Hero only: `.lockup-kicker` / `.lockup-title`
- Size scale tokens: `text-xs` … `text-7xl` (prefer roles over raw sizes in sections)
- `SectionHeader` composes eyebrow → heading → lead

**Controls**
- `Button` — `variant`: accent | ghost | link; `size`: sm | md | lg
- `DemoButton` — opens demo overlay; wraps `Button` (behavior only)
- `.chip` — selectable list row
- `Field` / `SelectField` — form controls

**Content keys** (generic, relevant)
- Shared: `eyebrow`, `title`, `body`
- Lists: `items` or `highlights` when that meaning fits
- FAQ: `question` / `answer`
- Testimonials: `quote`, `author`, `role`

Nav/menu/CTA labels stay uppercase (`Request a Demo`, `Log in`, `Menu`). Do not mention third-party reference sites in code, comments, or commit messages.

Delete unused components and copy when a page no longer needs them. Do not keep clinic/gym/multi-product scaffolding.
